cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or discuss this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "A Registry of Proto-Concepts with Referent Quarantine"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kapustin"
    given-names: "Igor"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-24"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/kapustin-i/proto-concept-registry"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - confabulation
  - negative confabulation
  - interpretability
  - naming
  - governance
  - proto-concepts
abstract: "A specification for an open registry of proto-concepts (machine-registered anomaly coordinates with provenance) coupled with a referent quarantine: a status system under which a registered entry may not be promoted to a working term until a reproducible behavioral test is attached and independently reproduced. Introduces negative confabulation: the failure mode in which a model, lacking a name for what is present, reports its absence."
